  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70822,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Head of the epididymis {25406742}</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70823,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients present in their third decade of life (age range: 12&ndash;81&nbsp;years) {20367315; 29154985; 4877911} with a painless, slowly growing scrotal swelling. Few cases cause pain. Uncommonly, the tumour is found during the workup of von&nbsp;Hippel&ndash;Lindau syndrome (VHL) or infertility {20367315}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70824,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Papillary cystadenoma can occur sporadically or as a manifestation of VHL. Papillary cystadenomas are unilateral in 60% of cases and bilateral in 40% of cases. Of the unilateral cases, 20.3% are associated with VHL. Of the bilateral cases, one third are associated with VHL {20367315; 23708309}. Only 1&nbsp;unilateral papillary cystadenoma was reported as an initial manifestation of VHL {29729363}. See also <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/36/297\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Von&nbsp;Hippel&ndash;Lindau syndrome</em> .</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70825,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology of sporadic cases is unknown. Familial cases are often a manifestation of VHL.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70826,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Papillary cystadenoma arises from VHL-associated maldeveloped mesonephric ductules (precursor lesions) coupled with a loss of the <em>VHL</em> allele {18813354}. Overexpression of angiogenic proteins like VEGF and HIF1 in the epithelial cells promotes vascular permeability, fluid accumulation, and cyst formation {9824115; 20367315}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70827,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are circumscribed, firm, and tan or grey-white, with glistening cut surfaces. The size ranges from 5&nbsp;to 80&nbsp;mm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70828,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Papillary processes and cysts are lined by cuboidal to columnar epithelial cells with small round nuclei and clear or vacuolated cytoplasm. Prominent cell borders and occasional cilia may be seen. Spaces between papillae and cysts contain deeply eosinophilic, homogeneous, colloid-like material. Cellular atypia, mitosis, and necrosis are absent, and the stroma is often fibrous with focal hyalinization {20367315}. Rare features include psammoma bodies, solid/nested growth, and focal reverse nuclear polarity with subnuclear vacuoles {4455175; 25406742}. The cells are immunoreactive for cytokeratin, AE1/AE3, CK7, PAX8, and CAIX with cup-like basolateral positivity; they are negative for CD10, calretinin, and WT1. Papillary cystadenoma has an immunoprofile similar to that of clear cell papillary renal cell tumour; positive CK7 and lectin histochemistry with negative CD10, AMACR, and RCCm argue against the latter {24441657; 17572225; 1694653; 23708309}. PAS stain may highlight cytoplasmic glycogen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70829,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A monotonous population of polygonal epithelial cells in sheets and multilayered groups is seen in papillary cystadenoma. Tumour cells contain eccentrically placed round or ovoid bland nuclei with ample pale or clear cytoplasm and without nucleoli or mitoses {31697443; 15192977}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70830,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In patients with VHL, loss of heterozygosity at 3p25-26 and <em>VHL</em> gene mutations at nucleotides 712, 713, and 694 have been demonstrated {8522307}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70831,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> epididymal location; papillary fronds with a fibrovascular core; bland morphology with clear cytoplasm; absence of features of malignancy.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> VHL association in bilateral cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70832,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70833,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 183,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Papillary cystadenoma is a benign tumour, and surgical excision is curative. One recurrence and two malignant transformations to cystadenocarcinoma have been reported {20367315; 25406742}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]